<h2>How Flood Insurance Works</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>NFIP policies</strong> are issued through FEMA&rsquo;s National Flood Insurance Program, often sold by private insurers. Building and contents coverage are separate, each with its own limit and deductible.</li>
<li><strong>Private flood policies</strong> may offer higher limits or different terms, such as additional living expenses. Terms vary by insurer.</li>
<li><strong>Waiting periods.</strong> NFIP coverage typically starts 30 days after purchase, with limited exceptions.</li>
<li><strong>Payment basis.</strong> Depending on the policy and occupancy, building damage may be paid at replacement cost or actual cash value, and contents are often paid at actual cash value. See <a href="/replacement-cost-vs-actual-cash-value-texas/">replacement cost vs. actual cash value</a>.</li>
</ul>

